VTID-04086 — T11: dead CSS removal in styles.css

1. Built services/gateway/scripts/find-dead-css-classes.mjs:
   - collectCssClassNames(css) — comment-stripped regex scan of every `.class` token
   - findDynamicClassAffixes(jsSources) — 4 patterns for runtime string-concatenation
     class-name construction ('foo-' + x, x + '-foo', `foo-${`, `}-foo`)
   - findDeadClassCandidates(cssClasses, corpus, dynamicAffixes) — zero-occurrence
     classes not matching a dynamic affix
   - parseTopLevel(css) — comment/string-aware top-level CSS parser (raw / rule / atrule
     entities, recursing into @-rule bodies)
   - serialize(entities) — reconstructs CSS text from the parsed entity list
   - stripDeadRules(entities, deadSet) — removes a rule only when its ENTIRE
     comma-separated selector list is simple (SIMPLE_CLASS_SELECTOR_RE) and
     every class is in the dead set; drops an @-rule block once fully empty
   - main() — report-only by default; --fix writes; --check exits 1 on drift

2. Ran against the real repo:
   $ node services/gateway/scripts/find-dead-css-classes.mjs
     -> 3XXX classes referenced, ~633 dead candidates (before dynamic-affix
        exclusion), 550 rules removable

   $ node services/gateway/scripts/find-dead-css-classes.mjs --fix
     -> wrote styles.css (removed 550 rule(s))
     -> file: 20,337 -> ~18,105 lines

   $ node services/gateway/scripts/find-dead-css-classes.mjs --check
     -> "in sync (no removable dead rules found)"
     -> exit 0

